<section id="getting-around" class="discovery-section"><div class="container guide-columns"><div><span class="eyebrow">Arrival &amp; transport</span><h2>Start with the right airport.</h2><p>Check your booking for the airport code. Antalya Airport (AYT) and Gazipaşa-Alanya Airport (GZP) serve different parts of the coast. Compare your accommodation’s actual location before choosing a transfer.</p><div id="cop31-airport-advisory" hidden><h3>Airport route advisory: 9–13 November 2026</h3><p>Antalya Airport asks passengers travelling during these dates to check its <a href="https://www.antalya-airport.aero/homepage" target="_blank" rel="noopener">COP31-related route advisory and linked official route information</a>, allow for possible traffic and plan departure accordingly. Confirm the current route before setting off; this notice does not identify specific road closures or guarantee journey times. Checked 11 November 2026. Dates are Antalya local time.</p></div><h3>From Antalya Airport</h3><p>The airport operator lists AntRay and bus connections. Confirm the route for your terminal and arrival time. For towns along the coast, plan the complete onward journey rather than assuming a direct service.</p><a class="text-link" href="https://www.antalya-airport.aero/passengers-visitors/transportation/buses-and-mass-transport" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Official airport transport information ↗</a><h3>Changing international terminals</h3><p>Checked on <time datetime="2026-11-10">10 November 2026</time>, <a href="https://www.antalya-airport.aero/passengers-visitors/transportation/transport-to-the-airport" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Antalya Airport's operator</a> describes a complimentary ring shuttle between <strong>International Terminal 1 and Terminal 2</strong>, with stops in front of each terminal's departures area.</p><p>The linked page does not publish shuttle frequency or operating hours. Confirm the current stop and service hours with the airport, and your flight's terminal with your airline, before relying on the shuttle. This is not a confirmed tram connection or a guarantee of service at your arrival time.</p><h3>Outside the city</h3><p>A hotel with “Antalya” in its address may be far from the city centre. Check the district, transfer length, pickup point and total price before booking. Mountain and coastal journeys deserve extra time.</p></div><aside class="planning-card"><h2>Useful official links</h2><a href="https://www.antalya-airport.aero/" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Antalya Airport (AYT) ↗</a><a href="https://gazipasa-airport.aero/" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Gazipaşa-Alanya Airport (GZP) ↗</a><a href="https://www.antalyakart.com.tr/" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Antalyakart transport information ↗</a><a href="https://www.mgm.gov.tr/" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Official weather &amp; warnings ↗</a><p class="source-note">Timetables and fares are deliberately linked, not copied: they can change.</p></aside></div></section>
<section id="itineraries" class="tint"><div class="container"><span class="eyebrow">Make it your own</span><h2>One, three or seven days.</h2><p>Editorial route ideas, not bookable tours. Adjust for opening days, weather, mobility and where you stay.</p><div class="experience-grid"><article class="experience-card"><span class="eyebrow">01 / City day</span><h3>A first taste of Antalya</h3><ol><li>Walk through <a href="/things-to-do/gate-of-hadrian/">Hadrian’s Gate</a> into Kaleiçi.</li><li>Leave time for lunch and the old harbour.</li><li>Finish at <a href="/things-to-do/karaalioglu-park/">Karaalioğlu Park</a>.</li></ol></article><article class="experience-card"><span class="eyebrow">03 / Short break</span><h3>City, coast, history</h3><ol><li>A slow day in Kaleiçi.</li><li><a href="/things-to-do/konyaalti-beach/">Konyaaltı</a> and a relaxed waterfront afternoon.</li><li>A planned excursion to <a href="/things-to-do/perge-ancient-city/">Perge</a> or Aspendos, depending on transport.</li></ol></article><article class="experience-card"><span class="eyebrow">07 / Room to wander</span><h3>Choose one direction</h3><ol><li>Spend your first two days in Antalya city.</li><li>Choose the western coast around Kemer/Kaş or the eastern coast around Side/Alanya.</li><li>Stay locally for three or four nights.</li><li>Keep a flexible final day for weather and your return journey.</li></ol></article></div></div></section>
<section id="essentials"><div class="container"><span class="eyebrow">Small details, better days</span><h2>Your practical checklist</h2><div class="guide-columns"><div class="faq-list"><details><summary>When should I visit?</summary><p>Use the <a href="/blog/antalya-weather-by-months-what-to-expect-before-you-visit/">monthly weather guide</a> for seasonal context. Check an official forecast and warnings for your actual dates. Sea, trail and boat conditions are never guaranteed by a monthly average.</p></details><details><summary>Can I visit Antalya Museum?</summary><p>The Ministry lists Antalya Museum as temporarily closed. Do not build a day around it without checking the <a href="https://kvmgm.ktb.gov.tr/TR-46782/gecici-sureyle-kapali-olan-muzeler-ve-bagli-birimler.html" target="_blank" rel="noopener">current official closure list</a>. Reviewed 9 November 2026.</p></details><details><summary>What about tickets, visas and entry rules?</summary><p>Check <a href="https://muze.gov.tr/" target="_blank" rel="noopener">official museum tickets</a> and <a href="https://www.evisa.gov.tr/" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Türkiye’s official e-Visa portal</a>. Entry rules depend on your nationality and documents. We do not sell visas or promise admission.</p></details><details><summary>What should I confirm with a hotel?</summary><p>Exact location, operating dates, room type, meal plan, cancellation terms, accessibility needs and whether facilities are seasonal. Our guide does not show live rates or inventory.</p></details></div><div class="planning-card"><h3>Travel thoughtfully</h3><p>Follow posted guidance at protected beaches and ancient sites. Keep wildlife undisturbed, take litter with you and avoid restricted trails or sea conditions beyond your ability.</p><a href="/events/">Check dates before buying tickets →</a><a href="/destinations/">Choose a realistic base →</a><a href="/sources/">Read our source policy →</a></div></div></div></section>

